# DEFAULT (2026-09-08, L60). Everything git detects as text is LF in the repository.
# This line must stay FIRST: .gitattributes is last-match-wins, so the explicit `binary`
# declarations below still override it for Office files, images and archives.
#
# It replaced an extension ENUMERATION, which was green and inert: it listed
# .sh/.py/.yml/.yaml/.json/.toml/.md and therefore silently allowed CRLF into
# policies/*.cedar (the input to the POLICY_VERSION provenance digest),
# tools/hooks/pre-commit (a bash script), lib/CORE_VERSION (hashed by lib/core.lock)
# and RELEASE. To be exact about the blast radius: the digests were NOT corrupted -
# verify_core._sha256 and _digest_of both collapse CRLF deliberately, and that was
# verified by CRLF-ifying both inputs and re-running. What CRLF actually cost was
# determinism and diff noise, which is enough.
#
# This file is SHARED (tools/check_doc_parity.py): all four packs must carry it
# byte-identical. Three different versions had already drifted when this was written -
# the L58 shape, copied by hand with nothing comparing the copies.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Prior history, kept because it explains why the enumeration existed at all.
# COPILOT-4 (2026-09-03), applied preventively: a script committed with CRLF fails on
# Linux (`set -euo pipefail\r`: "invalid option name"). *.md was added 2026-09-07 (L36)
# after a Markdown file that picked up CRLF showed as a 78-line whole-file diff with not
# one character of content different - noise that hides real evidence changes. The
# pharmacovigilance pack had no .gitattributes at all; neither did housing (found
# 2026-09-08, the third time).

# Office documents - ZIP archives. CRLF<->LF rewriting inside them strips embedded media
# and can make the file unopenable. `binary` = `-text -diff`.
*.pptx  binary
*.ppt   binary
*.docx  binary
*.doc   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary

# PDFs, images, archives, fonts
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary

# Text formats pinned to LF explicitly, so a reader of this file sees them named rather
# than only implied by `text=auto`.
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.cedar  text eol=lf
*.svg    text eol=lf
*.drawio text eol=lf
